  "description": "The 2026 election for Massachusetts's 1st Congressional District features longtime incumbent Democrat Richard Neal, who has held the seat since 2013 and previously represented the 2nd District from 1989. Neal, the top Democrat on the House Ways and Means Committee, faces a primary challenge from high school teacher Jeromie Whalen, who is running as a progressive opposing corporate PAC money and calling for generational change. Independent candidates Anthony Celata and Nadia Milleron are also in the race. The district, which covers western Massachusetts including Springfield, Pittsfield, and the Berkshires, is considered safely Democratic (Cook Political Report rates it Solid D).",
